h a test for every state-by-door cell. The callerless classifier and the duplicated client-only-time code are gone, the emitter string is deduplicated in all five places, and the proof's silent-failure message now reaches the terminal.\n\n**How big a deal.** Internal and reversible. Nothing touched staging or production. The branch is still `feat/*`, unlabelled, not draft, so it cannot route until you clear it.\n\n**What I need from you.** Nothing needed from you now. The manager runs review round 3; the bar it set was fewer than 10 findings with zero wrong-behaviour ones.\n\n**Two things worth knowing.**\n- I introduced one regression mid-round and caught it by running the whole test suite: closing the sheet after every write made an existing \"a different verb is still available\" test flaky. It was fixed in a separate commit and disclosed at the top of the PR comment.\n- I did not score the discipline scoreboard or log. That file is the manager's, and two sessions clobbered it once before. The per-finding verify-and-bucket read is in the PR comment for the manager to transcribe. I also left the dispatch brief alone for the same reason.\n\n**Details.** The PR comment carries the evidence the brief demanded: the red reproductions at `b686578`, the 3-state by 10-door table, the void check at 45 of 45 guarded (filed), the item-20 stdout/stderr table for the proof, the migration-reissue, operator-artifacts and claim-drift outputs, all nine mutation modes still caught, the full vitest suite green (202 files, 3323 tests), coverage floor, both CI job step lists including the two proofs fix round 1 had skipped locally, fresh-db, the lab shots read, and contrast at zero under the floor. The PR body was re-issued and read back byte-identical apart from a trailing newline.","ttft_ms":3484,"type":"result","duration_ms":1282758,"uuid":"87be7ca5-5f3f-4292-9398-ec67a6e58695","ttft_stream_ms":1387,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":1387,"queued_turn_count":0,"result